@0    = ~<CHARNAME>, there is something I must speak with you about - in private.~
@1    = ~I cannot help noticing that our companion Faren's eyes are drawn frequently to you. Of course, I understand that you...invoke feelings in others, but I would appreciate it if you made our relationship clear.~
@2    = ~I am sorry, Ajantis. Things changed since Irenicus: I like Faren, now.~
@3    = ~There is none. Faren is a simple companion and nothing more.~
@4    = ~Thank you, my love. I love you with all my soul, and it was not my intention to reproach you with this. Still, you have set my heart easy.~
@5    = ~Be careful, Faren. I have seen your glances at Lady <CHARNAME>, and they are not proper for a man of your habits.~
@6    = ~What kind of habits would those be? Exactly?~
@7    = ~You carouse and you gamble. Not to mention your - ahem - dalliances with women and men of doubtful virtue.~
@8    = ~Ha! That's the dumbest thing I've heard in a while. Thanks for the entertainment, but--~
@9    = ~I am not finished.~
@10   = ~Oh - okay. I'm sorry.~
@11   = ~<CHARNAME> deserves a loved one who can cherish her all her life, who will stay at her side and understand her every thought. Can you do that?~
@12   = ~<CHARNAME>, there is something I would like to speak with you about.~
@13   = ~It is about Faren's conduct of late. I understand that you...invoke feelings in others, even our travelling companions, but I wish to know whether there is any regard on your side.~
@14   = ~I do enjoy Faren's company, and consider him more than a friend.~
@15   = ~I...understand, <CHARNAME>. Thank you for clarifying the situation.~
@16   = ~It's good having a guy like you around. Makes the rest of us look a bit more reputable, heh.~
@17   = ~Ha! I have nae desire t' look reputable, laddie! Warriors like us need nae such thing!~
@18   = ~That is not the purpose of my journeying with the group, as you well know.~
@19   = ~Oh, I know - was just making conversation. Didn't mean to step on any toes, just...~
@20   = ~Isn't it a bit weird hanging around with, well, people like me? Ordinary people?~
@21   = ~Not at all. Besides, the work of a paladin is not to be merely extraordinary. It is to show the light of Helm to our companions, in order that they may better themselves.~
@22   = ~So, what you're saying is you stealth-convert people? Never knew paladins were so sneaky!~
@23   = ~No, that is not what I--~
@24   = ~No, no - it's a brilliant idea. You feel free to convert me any day, Ajantis!~
@25   = ~Must you keep whistling that tune, Faren? I will have it going around my head all <DAYNIGHT>, now.~
@26   = ~I've been trying to get it of mine - I could sing it, if you like. Might get it out quicker.~
@27   = ~I have heard you sing when you wash the crockery, and though I am sure it is, er, pleasant for you to do so, I do not--~
@28   = ~No need to worry over my feelings, Ajantis. I'm as tone-deaf as an upside-down cow, always have been.~
@29   = ~Plus, you might not approve of the words. There are some...not particularly knightly verses. Don't worry, I'll keep quiet.~
@30   = ~Hey, Ajantis, come have a drink. C'mon, it'll be fun. See a bit of the world...~
@31   = ~I have no wish to see any such world. Why people choose to drown themselves in such places is beyond my understanding.~
@32   = ~Besides, I believe you're in no condition to see straight at all. Follow my hand with your eyes.~
@33   = ~Uh, which one? You got three of them...~
@34   = ~Best get to bed, Faren, so we can be in a fit state at <CHARNAME>'s side tomorrow.~
